  {"title": "Convergence and limit",
   "text":
   "A sequence converges to x if, for every ε > 0, there exists an M such that all terms with n ≥ M are within ε of x. A sequence is convergent when it has a limit.",
   "target": "Filter.Tendsto s Filter.atTop (nhds x)",
   "structured":
   {"type": "\\mathbb{R}",
